# CR 701.27f for a triggered ability: a permanent's own ability transforms it only if it hasn't transformed since the
# ability was put onto the stack. Panharmonicon makes Dowsing Device's entering trigger twice (CR 603.2d). Both resolve
# with five artifacts on the battlefield, then four once the Device is Geode Grotto (a land): Sol Ring, Mox Ruby, Mox
# Pearl and Panharmonicon, so "if you control four or more artifacts" holds for each. The first turns the Device into
# Geode Grotto; the second finds it has transformed since that ability went on the stack, and the land stays Geode
# Grotto rather than turning back into Dowsing Device.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Sol Ring
Panharmonicon
Dowsing Device
Mountain
Mountain x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Panharmonicon.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dowsing Device.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Triggers(Dowsing Device; Dowsing Device)
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Geode Grotto.Types = Land
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl; Sol Ring; Panharmonicon; Geode Grotto
Bot1.Battlefield.Geode Grotto.Types = Land
